      "notes": "Desktop monitor controller. Four stereo analogue sources: SRC 1 and SRC 2 and a dedicated Cue input, all balanced on 1/4\" TRS, plus an unbalanced Aux on RCA and a 3.5 mm mini jack, where plugging into the mini jack overrides the RCA. The Alt input adds optical and coaxial S/PDIF up to 192 kHz. Three stereo speaker outputs (Main, Alt 1, Alt 2) and an assignable mono sub output, all balanced on 1/4\" TRS. Four headphone outputs: HP1 is the monitor-grade one on the front, HP2 to HP4 are foldback and sit on the rear. Talkback runs off an internal microphone or the rear XLR, which a rear switch sets to dynamic or 48 V. No power draw is quoted: the 12 V centre-positive supply is rated 2 A, which is the adapter's ceiling rather than what the unit takes.",
